#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/id #uuid "3f141210-8194-5346-9e2a-c47f98bb3443" :question/math-academy-id "e-10840" :question/problem "Compute $P\\left( X > 8 \\right)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n![](images/85/8507c337ea73575abbc2127507f2b0ae8440b3587bf0191fe7344b8be6dfb1b3.svg)" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a <    X <    b) = \\int_a^b f(x) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }5{e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-5x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-40}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Constant Given a PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "d40a67bd-7d98-58fb-b4a1-7a556e91556a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10851" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n![](images/48/48acd7d6ad8f581ba6033e19282fca0e43019c06ec2812c0698e50edd81075d6.svg)" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x) = \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3}$ on the interval $x \\geq 0,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\infty} \\dfrac{k}{(4x+1)^3} \\, \\textrm dx = 1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{k}{(4x+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{[\\frac{k}{8(4x+1)^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{8} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad k = 8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192535 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "5f988175-cdd9-5ddf-94b5-3b995dc75fce" :question/math-academy-id "e-12329" :question/problem "![](images/15/1562da3da10e26ab9b4aff6adaa71fcbb1c2de963b4bfc682663f7fcfa62f8d6.svg)\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\geq 3$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{3}^{\\infty} f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x = 1$\n\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x) \\geq 0$ for all $x \\in S$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\int_{S} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x \\geq 3,$ we have $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2} \\geq 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }(x-2)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c322e5-829f-50a2-ad6c-a37c8ed639b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259929} {:answer/id #uuid "0e82cf90-740a-58be-9b33-ff712c7c0b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260016} {:answer/id #uuid "2c71cf0b-9bd2-52e1-928e-2f90eba7ffd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260279} {:answer/id #uuid "aa77c3af-2f33-5c17-86df-cf59ab7210ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261375} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3baac4-1b9b-5b5c-a181-fc7767384433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa77c3af-2f33-5c17-86df-cf59ab7210ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261375} :answer-field/id #uuid "62001f44-b72f-57e0-ac60-fab7e1401c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ea64e3a-0876-5727-96dc-6cee351571a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126032" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(2\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }2{e}^{2-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{2-2x}]}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f82104-dc7d-57c3-98d6-01a9c65196e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408058} {:answer/id #uuid "322e2b30-d710-51d2-8606-8bee18140367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408059} {:answer/id #uuid "59ad5255-5a70-5c33-9335-d0a5e5d59557" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408063} {:answer/id #uuid "6249b9e8-0127-5eee-876d-bd9fe3be9480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408064} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d72fdb-d63f-5f10-a2b0-b041b91327b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6249b9e8-0127-5eee-876d-bd9fe3be9480" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408064} :answer-field/id #uuid "d77bfd50-03ce-5cb3-a091-5ba8b32f073a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46ac655-a97e-50cb-a022-2af841ed15e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160451" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 1$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 1,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{{x}^{8}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{7}}\\,{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278311 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192807 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "441a1de0-dc64-59fe-99a8-0ab502841425" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Whether a Given Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34724edc-a4ca-5e89-a69c-bacffe903e41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275951} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8e282f-89cb-53a8-9e64-f63d069a13a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276026} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2ddccb-4b30-5b76-ac15-d6c563dfdc53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276293} {:answer/id #uuid "6e37991d-b419-53b8-b775-152586dd4890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276470} {:answer/id #uuid "a34f0ce9-1a9c-5f93-aaa6-3c868738beef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e8e282f-89cb-53a8-9e64-f63d069a13a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276026} :answer-field/id #uuid "4646bb7e-6a09-5531-8391-f1f097bfe6dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3e574537-84e0-52ce-b8da-3afe1320a385" :question/math-academy-id "q-160459" :question/problem "$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven the function $f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\ge 0$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for $x\\ge 0,$ we have $f(x)=\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\ge 0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{(3x+1)^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(3x+1)^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statements I and II are true, the first and second conditions are satisfied. So, $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Constant Given a PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "424bed6b-ca8e-56d1-b2ba-317bd14a5d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276064} {:answer/id #uuid "65893455-9ff5-5860-b552-578c64631415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276393} {:answer/id #uuid "69678a60-bb17-5433-b8bd-0dcfaf8f242a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276429} {:answer/id #uuid "b9bb89d7-3d9d-5a9e-93a3-f4cbd807ef5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277130} {:answer/id #uuid "cf43676d-e669-59cb-a36a-466aeb9d25ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "424bed6b-ca8e-56d1-b2ba-317bd14a5d4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276064} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a54ad9f-1c7c-5c9d-b381-6d0caba02b7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277800}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21dab0f5-e122-5ef2-bac0-e65430de8846" :question/math-academy-id "q-160469" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{2-x},\\, & x\\ge -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{2-x}$ on the interval $x\\ge -1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\infty }k{e}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}x=-k{e}^{2-x}\\,{|}_{-1}^{\\infty }=k{e}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk{e}^{3}=1\\,⟹\\,k={e}^{-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193398 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192760 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44034972-5d1f-5833-9415-2cd62da27891" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352199} {:answer/id #uuid "48b14eee-c397-5b3a-bbde-437ae5b44dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352242} {:answer/id #uuid "598b16fd-1efc-50d1-a858-b6a88ba1c0c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352363} {:answer/id #uuid "95ecc404-9569-54c3-a1aa-0054028eafc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352871} {:answer/id #uuid "9a1d2d32-6223-5ff2-b0e1-73f1f39e0d50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48b14eee-c397-5b3a-bbde-437ae5b44dfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352242} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d0a1e6-3385-5385-80a6-56bd97e8139e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9869c64e-9e23-5b9b-b7d6-0c4c49a322f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-86918" :question/problem "Compute $P(X>8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =P(8<X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{x}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd8455e1-46f3-5956-80ec-e6753cc005a7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Constant Given a PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ff9cf6-5fcf-5d3c-80e8-703c37214290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408060} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1b0a3a-bdbd-5374-b104-778a4895bbcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408061} {:answer/id #uuid "54155b31-f5d8-5461-b182-f36b15f21107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408062} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4fce9d-6645-5493-9cd5-fa793878e3c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408065} {:answer/id #uuid "febc2157-abdf-56d9-ac62-6e6fbc37e416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54155b31-f5d8-5461-b182-f36b15f21107" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408062} :answer-field/id #uuid "d55ee039-24b2-5902-95f1-72edb9d13725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53d894bf-6308-5f50-b4d9-b3439fc6a9bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-87239" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-8x},\\, & x>0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{-8x}$ on the interval $0<x<\\infty ,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }k{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x={[-\\frac{k}{8}{e}^{-8x}]}_{0}^{\\infty }=\\frac{k}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{k}{8}=1\\,⟹\\,k=8.\n$$"}]}
